{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"422a615dcce2626e87c735bd3cf9079cf3e60583db92d9a4fa7c3aba1697cd60","digest":{"component_or_area":"metrics adapters","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/adapters/github_actions.py","scripts/harvest_gha.py","tests/unit/metrics/test_gha_adapter.py",".rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson","src/rebar/metrics/snapshot.py","src/rebar/metrics/registry.py","src/rebar/metrics/__init__.py",".github/workflows/test.yml","pytest-cov TOTAL line"],"problem_keywords":["coverage harvesting","CI-health metrics","GitHub Actions integration","snapshot persistence","metric adapters","log parsing"],"propositions":["Coverage % and CI-health metrics from GitHub Actions runs must be harvested from the GHA API and run logs after the fact and persisted to the tracked `.rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson` store to survive the GHA short log-retention window.","The GHA adapter must extract coverage % via word-boundary grep for the pytest-cov TOTAL line in run-log tail and compute red->green recovery intervals from fail→pass run pairs via run-metadata JSON.","The harvester script and GHA adapter must remain isolated from the core metrics command and registry modules to maintain portability and enable future non-GHA CI adapters.","Snapshots written by the harvester must be labeled with `source=\"snapshot\"` or CI-health-specific labels and appended to the durable tracked store, not to the gitignored `reports/` directory."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787573155735202001,"uuid":"ff7c17b3-d280-49ad-a7ab-6bbb651a6fd7"}